-        <p>Located between the South China Sea and the Pacific Ocean, the Philippines' threat perceptions have spiked. In response, it is accelerating efforts to modernise its military and cultivate its security partnerships with Washington and others. It is also expanding ties with other countries to draw even with more militarily advanced neighbours and hedge against scenarios in which the White House downgrades its commitment to its Asian allies.</p>
